# Industry Differentiators: Manufacturing — Overview

## Four Core Strengths

### 1. OT/IT Convergence
- MES integration (Siemens Opcenter, Rockwell FactoryTalk, GE Proficy)
- Shop-floor connectivity (MQTT, OPC-UA, Ignition SCADA)
- Edge computing (Azure IoT Edge, AWS Greengrass)
- **Proof**: 99.97% uptime for manufacturing environment where 5 min = $50K

### 2. Regulatory Compliance
- FDA 21 CFR Part 11 (pharmaceutical)
- ISO 13485 (medical devices)
- ITAR/EAR (export-controlled data)
- EPA reporting and sustainability
- **Proof**: SOX-compliant financials with zero audit findings

### 3. Supply Chain Integration
- ERP-to-supplier portal integration (Coupa, Ariba, SAP SRM)
- Demand planning connected to shop-floor scheduling
- Quality integration (non-conformance → supplier corrective action)
- **Proof**: Reduced order-to-delivery from 14 days to 6 days

### 4. Predictive Maintenance
- Azure Digital Twins for production line modeling
- ML models achieving 85% bearing failure prediction accuracy
- Real-time monitoring with automated work order creation
- **Proof**: Prevented $2.3M in unplanned downtime (first 18 months)

## Competitive Positioning

| Competitor Type | Their Weakness | Our Advantage |
|----------------|--------------|---------------|
| Big 4 | Junior teams, high turnover | Senior-only, consistent team |
| Cloud Boutiques | No manufacturing knowledge | 40+ manufacturing engagements |
| System Integrators | Product-first | Business-outcome focused |
| Offshore-Only | Timezone challenges | Hybrid onshore/nearshore |

## Statistics
- 40+ manufacturing clients since 2015
- $380M+ in manufacturing implementations
- 98% client retention in manufacturing
- 15 manufacturing-specific accelerators

## Win/Loss Patterns in Manufacturing
- **Win**: Speed to value, specialization, fixed-price certainty
- **Lose**: Brand prestige at Fortune 500 (McKinsey, Accenture)
- **Strategy**: Lead with technical accelerators, ROI proof points
